{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403398-mask-of-a-thousand-faces-does-this-apply-to-objects-on-your-person","id":1403398,"title":"Mask of A thousand Faces; Does this apply to objects on your person?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-18T10:08:16-07:00","id":1403398,"title":"Mask of A thousand Faces; Does this apply to objects on your person?","content":"I was wondering if one could use MoaTF to change the appearance of your clothes, the model of your gun, perhaps even fool others by masking ID cards (Yes, I'm aware that that's Chimestry's territory) and the forum's take on such things. I think, somewhere, I read that Settites wear animal masks and use Thousand faces to make these seem like the real thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T11:11:32-07:00","id":1403402,"title":"","content":"In pre-V5, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T11:11:57-07:00","id":1403403,"title":"","content":"Weapons no for certain. There was an advanced power for obfuscate that let you hold a great sword and it could appear as a rose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T13:14:16-07:00","id":1403413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403398-mask-of-a-thousand-faces-does-this-apply-to-objects-on-your-person?p=1403402#post1403402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In pre-V5, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is not a v5 thread<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pnizzle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403398-mask-of-a-thousand-faces-does-this-apply-to-objects-on-your-person?p=1403403#post1403403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weapons no for certain. There was an advanced power for obfuscate that let you hold a great sword and it could appear as a rose.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really a power for extreme absurdities, not your normal stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T14:19:45-07:00","id":1403418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pnizzle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403398-mask-of-a-thousand-faces-does-this-apply-to-objects-on-your-person?p=1403403#post1403403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weapons no for certain. There was an advanced power for obfuscate that let you hold a great sword and it could appear as a rose.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I remember c., the sword still appear as a sword but people don't make drama about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T21:35:57-07:00","id":1403483,"title":"","content":"I don't think it ever said specifically in the books. In the games I've played in and run, we've let it hide weapons if it's part of the disguise, like a shotgun as a cane when making myself look like a little old man. I guess it's pretty much up to ST interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T21:53:47-07:00","id":1403484,"title":"","content":"Pre-V5 there was a 6th level ability called &quot;Conceal Weapon&quot; that hides a weapon from sight even if you attack with it. So it could technically be melded into a disguise as another item if you want to flavor it that way.<br /> <br /> But no, Mask of a Thousand Faces only affects your own appearance and mannerisms. It wouldn't affect weapons or other inanimate objects such as clothes or a physical ID card.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T22:02:07-07:00","id":1403486,"title":"","content":"What book was conceal weapon from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T22:06:00-07:00","id":1403487,"title":"","content":"Player's guide to Low Clans, page 150","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-18T22:18:20-07:00","id":1403488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kael03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403398-mask-of-a-thousand-faces-does-this-apply-to-objects-on-your-person?p=1403487#post1403487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Player's guide to Low Clans, page 150</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah that explains it. I was out of the game for a good while around then up till a few years ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T00:23:51-07:00","id":1403493,"title":"","content":"Regarding clothes; If a 150kg muscle-vampire turns into a tiny 50kg person, Is the XS illusion wearing XL clothes, are those clothes refited but somehow the vampire can't conciously change them, or can the vampire just change the appearance of these clothes to match what people think the tiny person would wear? I feel like if I can make this drastic change to my person, I should at least be able to change clothes (if at a higher number of successes) <br /> <br /> But that said, the V20 book omits talking about clothes and I don't know if that's deliberate or an oversight. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kael03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403398-mask-of-a-thousand-faces-does-this-apply-to-objects-on-your-person?p=1403484#post1403484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pre-V5 there was a 6th level ability called &quot;Conceal Weapon&quot; that hides a weapon from sight even if you attack with it. So it could technically be melded into a disguise as another item if you want to flavor it that way.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>but that's very extreme. IE I think you can stab someone with this power and they won't really become aware that your flower is a sword. The &quot;thing&quot; of that power seems that you can make an outlandish change that people believe despite suspension of disbelief breaking down. Changing, say, A Glock pistol into looking like a Browning pistol isn't going to harm your suspension of disbelief: you have a different model of a 9mm pistol that still fires 9mm, that's less significant than, say, making myself a short black female, or making an ordinary looking vampire look like MyWife. <br /> <br /> Obfuscate tends to break when move to murder attempt of someone because, just like you can't dominate someone to kill themselves, they won't ignore you lining up their execution. Changing a sword into a flower would need it's own elder power because it's in violation of this principle, changing one pistol into another wouldn't make a difference concerning this principle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T03:27:38-07:00","id":1403507,"title":"","content":"I would let <i>Mask of a Thousand Faces</i> work with clothes, if for no other reason than because I love the image of an Elder vampire who walks around naked, with only Obfuscate clothing. Basically a vampiric Emperor's New Clothes.<br /> <br /> I say an Elder, since their Obfuscate will be high enough that only Auspex 5 vampires will be able to see through their clothe-less-ness.<br /> <br /> It's probably either a Malkavian - who legitimately thinks they're wearing the finest clothing, and uses Obfuscate to sell the illusion - or a Nosferatu, who wants to fuck with people. Just <i>daring</i> anyone who can see their nudity to say anything about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T04:22:33-07:00","id":1403508,"title":"","content":"Obfuscate does not affect your appearance, your weapons or your clothes. It only affects the minds of the onlookers.<br /> That said, you need a higher skill in obfuscate to pull of the more difficult manipulations.<br /> More successes means more control. More skill means more effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26274-moriaki","name":"Moriaki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26274_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T05:40:40-07:00","id":1403512,"title":"","content":"Welcome to the boards Moriaki!<br /> <br /> Mask affects clothing. If you are wearing high heels and a mini dress and you mask yourself into a football player it would kind of give it away. Also Nosfuratu crawl out of sewers and trick pretty people to sleep and feed them sometimes even embracing the vain as punishment only to drop the veil and be a rag covered monster, so I'd say it's cannon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24221-vamps-like-us","name":"Vamps Like Us","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T06:14:35-07:00","id":1403517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moriaki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1403398-mask-of-a-thousand-faces-does-this-apply-to-objects-on-your-person?p=1403508#post1403508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obfuscate does not affect your appearance, your weapons or your clothes. It only affects the minds of the onlookers.<br /> That said, you need a higher skill in obfuscate to pull of the more difficult manipulations.<br /> More successes means more control. More skill means more effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's true that MoaTF does not really change the clothes one wears or their face but it affects how people look at them, basically they believe what you want them to believe. You can look like anyone you want (but you don't get more temporary dots in charisma even if you force others to believe you are a supermodel) because those who look at you see you that way despite you not really looking that way at all. So if you use MoaTF to appear like someone else you have spent time studying (and rolled enough successes obviously) the people looking at you will think they see that person and will ignore evidence to the contrary including mismatching or absent ID cards (also subject to good rolls to avoid raising suspicion). Keep in mind that obfuscate fools onlookers but does not fool surveliance devices. A videocamera recording will show an obfuscated nosferatu passing behind a guard post in a military base for example (unless the vampire notices the camera, which means he/she rolls well on an awareness check, and then rolls well on a stealth check to avoid the camera recording him/her entering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T09:09:59-07:00","id":1403824,"title":"","content":"So the more I think about it the less conceal weapon makes sense as a level 6 power. With level 5 (v20) you can use any of the lower levels of obfuscate on a group (including mask of 1000 faces) and one of the other level 6 powers, Conceal, let's you hide an entire house or even a moving vehicle. You should at least be able to hide a weapon with lower levels or use other Conceal, which is much less narrow in scope than conceal weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T13:18:50-07:00","id":1403876,"title":"","content":"Mask of a Thousand Faces has always been based on the number of successes rolled. One success barely makes you look different, and it's possible to still be identified. Two successes you appear kind of different, but observers don't agree on what you look like! Only at three successes do you succeed in looking like a specific kind of different person - but it's only appearance, and other things could give the vampire away (the vampire's voice, a limp, a distinct way of walking, etc.). Additional successes expand on that, making your body language, voice, and mannerisms be appropriate. At five successes you begin to get away with very advance changes - different sex, different body type, etc.<br /> <br /> So an ST must use that as a guideline. In general, Mask works well if you want to blend into a crowd, and works much less when trying to pose as a specific individual, especially with more specific details. The more changes you want, the more successes you need.<br /> <br /> So for the appearance of clothes, I would allow that at either four or five successes based on the type of change. Perhaps even more if the difference in clothes is very strong (say t-shirt and shorts and sandals into an expensive brand name suit and dress shoes - better get six or more successes). <br /> <br /> I wouldn't allow Driver's ID to change except at 6 or more successes. And while I might allow the ID to work for something minor, like a bouncer or bartender checking the ID for age at 6 successes, for it to pass a thorough examination like a police officer who is trained to spot fake IDs, I'd require even more. And of course, any independent tests that don't require an observing mind to work, will outright fail (like running the ID against a database). For all practical purposes, vampires can't be using this power to do it. It'll fail most of the time.<br /> <br /> Every ST will have their own comfort zone on what they allow at each level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}